  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cooperation BIRN Albania Strategy 2026-2030</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Samarbete BIRN Albaniens strategi 2026&#x2013;2030</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Strengthening independent and innovative journalism that informs citizens and expands access to verified information;
- Enhancing rule of law, governance and democratic accountability through open data and evidence-based monitoring;
- Advancing human rights, media freedom and information integrity amid rapid digital transformation; and
- Building organisational resilience, learning and sustainability to secure long-term impact and independence.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Detta &#xe4;r k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;det f&#xf6;r BIRN Albaniens strategi 2026&#x2013;2030. Strategin bygger p&#xe5; BIRN Albaniens erfarenhet inom gr&#xe4;vande journalistik, publicering av &#xf6;ppna data, policy&#xf6;vervakning och medborgerligt samarbete. Den konsoliderar organisationens dubbla roll som vakthund och kunskapsnav, och &#xf6;verbryggar klyftan mellan medborgare och institutioner genom att omvandla komplex data och offentlig information till tillg&#xe4;nglig bevisning som st&#xf6;djer informerade beslut. J&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och inkludering, milj&#xf6;m&#xe4;ssig h&#xe5;llbarhet och digital etik &#xe4;r integrerade i redaktionellt arbete, partnerskap och organisationsstyrning.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is core support to BIRN Albania Strategy 2026-2030. The Strategy builds on BIRN Albania&#x2019;s experience in investigative journalism, open-data publishing, policy monitoring and civic collaboration. It consolidates the organisation&#x2019;s dual role as a watchdog and knowledge hub, bridging the gap between citizens and institutions by transforming complex data and public information into accessible evidence that supports informed decision-making.
Gender equality and inclusion, environmental sustainability, and digital ethics are mainstreamed across editorial work, partnerships, and organisational governance.</narrative>
  </description>
